# QueueLess++ Environment Variables
#
# Copy to apps/api/.env for local dev. The API and the BullMQ worker
# (`npm run worker`) read the same file and must point at the same Mongo
# and Redis instances.
#
# ── Production checklist (architecture doc §14) ───────────────────────
#  [ ] NODE_ENV=production
#  [ ] MONGODB_URI      → a replica set / Atlas (transactions require it)
#  [ ] REDIS_URL        → rediss:// (TLS); same instance for API + worker
#  [ ] SESSION_COOKIE_SECRET → a long unique random value, NOT the dev
#                              placeholder below (startup hard-fails in
#                              production if it's left unchanged)
#  [ ] FRONTEND_URL     → only used for CORS in the two-process dev
#                         setup and for links in outbound emails; in a
#                         single-origin deploy set it to the deployed
#                         origin so email links resolve
#  [ ] RESEND_API_KEY + RESEND_FROM_EMAIL → real email delivery
#      (omit both → transactional/reminder emails are only logged)
#  [ ] GEMINI_API_KEY   → enables no-show risk scoring (optional; unset
#                         means the job silently no-ops)
#  [ ] Build the frontend (`npm run build` in apps/web) so the API
#      serves apps/web/dist same-origin; otherwise it runs API-only.

# Backend
PORT=4000
NODE_ENV=development

# Database — must be a replica set (Mongo transactions are used throughout)
MONGODB_URI=

# Redis / Upstash — sessions, booking holds, rate limiters
REDIS_URL=

# Authentication — Redis-backed opaque sessions (HttpOnly cookie), not JWT
SESSION_COOKIE_SECRET=
SESSION_TTL_SECONDS=604800
MAGIC_LINK_TTL_SECONDS=3600

# CORS origin for the frontend dev server (local dev only — production is
# single-origin, architecture doc Section 14, so this only matters while
# frontend/backend run as two separate dev processes). Also used as the
# base for links in outbound emails.
FRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:5173

# AI — no-show risk scoring (architecture doc §10). Leave GEMINI_API_KEY unset to
# disable scoring entirely: the job no-ops silently and noShowRiskNote stays null.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# Optional — defaults to gemini-1.5-flash
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-1.5-flash

# Email (Resend) — leave both unset in local dev to use the console-log stub sender
RESEND_API_KEY=
RESEND_FROM_EMAIL=

# Frontend calls the API via relative /api/... paths (see apps/web/src/lib/api.ts and
# apps/web/vite.config.ts's dev proxy) — no frontend-side API base-URL variable is needed.
